// Minimal PDF text extractor — zero dependencies, works in Node (>=18) and
// workerd. Non-OCR: extracts text from PDF text operators (Tj/TJ/'/") in page
// content streams. Scanned/image PDFs have no text operators → empty pages.
//
// Strategy:
//   1. Scan raw bytes (latin1) for "N 0 obj ... endobj" objects.
//   2. Walk /Root → /Pages → /Kids (recursive) to get real page order.
//   3. Resolve each page's /Contents ref(s); inflate FlateDecode streams via
//      DecompressionStream('deflate') (zlib format, exactly what PDF uses).
//   4. Lex content streams for text-showing operators, honoring Td/TD/T* to
//      emit line breaks.
//
// Limits: 5 MB input, 100 pages. Unsupported encodings (non-CID custom fonts)
// may yield garbage — we extract what is readable and mark the rest honestly.

